# CLI Todo Application

A simple command-line interface todo application with in-memory storage, built with Python 3.13.

## Features

- Add tasks with title and optional description
- List all tasks with status indicators
- Update task details by ID
- Delete tasks by ID
- Toggle task completion status
- Interactive REPL interface

## Setup

1. Ensure you have Python 3.13 installed
2. Install the project dependencies using `uv`:
   ```bash
   uv venv
   uv pip install -e .
   ```

## Usage

To start the CLI application, run:

```bash
python -m src.main
```

Or if you have the package installed:
```bash
todo
```

## Available Commands

- `add "Title" "Description"` - Add a new task with title and optional description
  Example: `add "Buy groceries" "Milk, eggs, bread"`

- `list` or `ls` - Show all tasks with their status
  Example: `list`

- `update ID "Title" "Description"` - Update the title and/or description of a task
  Example: `update 1 "Updated title" "Updated description"`

- `delete ID` or `del ID` - Remove a task by ID
  Example: `delete 1`

- `done ID` or `toggle ID` - Mark a task as complete/incomplete
  Example: `done 1`

- `help` or `?` - Show available commands
  Example: `help`

- `exit` - Exit the application
  Example: `exit`

## Example Session

```
Welcome to the Todo App!
Type 'help' for available commands or 'exit' to quit.

> add "Buy groceries" "Milk, eggs, bread"
Task added with ID: 1
> add "Call mom"
Task added with ID: 2
> list
Your tasks:
1. [❌] Buy groceries
    Milk, eggs, bread
2. [❌] Call mom
> done 1
Task 1 marked as completed
> list
Your tasks:
1. [✅] Buy groceries
    Milk, eggs, bread
2. [❌] Call mom
> exit
Goodbye!
```

## Architecture

The application follows a clean architecture pattern with separation of concerns:

- `models.py` - Contains the Task data model
- `storage.py` - Implements the InMemoryTodoService with all CRUD operations
- `cli.py` - Handles command parsing and user interface
- `main.py` - Application entry point
